# Roots added to ESP-IDF's certificate bundle (sdkconfig.defaults, CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CUSTOM_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE).
#
# updates.acgt.net's certificate is from Let's Encrypt's Gen Y hierarchy (intermediate YE1 under
# ISRG Root YE). ESP-IDF 5.3.2's bundle predates Gen Y: boards verify the site today only because
# its chain carries cross-signs up to ISRG Root X2 and X1. If Let's Encrypt drops those from its
# default chain, as it did with DST Root X3 in 2021, boards without these roots could no longer
# fetch OTA updates, and could only be fixed over serial.
#
# From https://letsencrypt.org/certificates/ (gen-y/root-ye.pem, gen-y/root-yr.pem). Each was checked
# to be self-signed and to have the same key as Let's Encrypt's cross-sign of it (root-ye-by-x2,
# root-yr-by-x1), which verifies against ISRG Root X2 / X1 from ESP-IDF's own bundle.
#
# ISRG Root YE (ECDSA P-384), valid to 2045-09-02
# SHA-256 E1:4F:FC:AD:5B:00:25:73:10:06:CA:A4:3A:12:1A:22:D8:E9:70:0F:4F:B9:CF:85:2F:02:A7:08:AA:5D:56:66
